signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"9eecd75992bd49b4c2902485a2810b345c15c8bf2b6cb200aa37a6e41c35d88b","event_uuid":"1a6317c6-84ab-4de1-93ce-33fecd8f2819","position":{"commit_sha":"e0984aee9e6cb2ff4f8815f5c19171b626085bd2","position":"1793810809818155001-1a6317c6-84ab-4de1-93ce-33fecd8f2819"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"a241fe2bb4f5d852d3f806b6457cd3e19b8345b645e397dd0cd8f4b18af91507","event_uuid":"69021b9d-08e5-4782-ae7f-cd071467185f","position":{"commit_sha":"8d2d39f5c97b43f16648a2b3952e6dad72263313","position":"1793810852351362001-69021b9d-08e5-4782-ae7f-cd071467185f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"a08366aa6f8b2ace2a6db47e07e9ceb9f01ff22e814d7b032d156a869ab377f3","event_uuid":"a75094f7-c402-4392-8132-81f00515eabb","position":{"commit_sha":"8d2d39f5c97b43f16648a2b3952e6dad72263313","position":"1793810861990542001-a75094f7-c402-4392-8132-81f00515eabb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"9e4c6329e1d0ae4fa07b61ec8e8b4f185cf39aaf0a893afb44b7b0eacc20e538","event_uuid":"8126e3fe-96b8-494c-a404-894a9266cbe5","position":{"commit_sha":"250e86819e3cf55e85613ee675ee75240311bb07","position":"1793811682957127001-8126e3fe-96b8-494c-a404-894a9266cbe5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"bbf28752b7fa31cc51714408f754e3ef2a8f24e4a25b9646ad78ed1e889ffb3d","event_uuid":"9ec08129-ccd8-4ef0-bf1e-55b8dba180a7","position":{"commit_sha":"af72ce8a8493cbc130eeb3262818e7d976c828dc","position":"1793812279825385001-9ec08129-ccd8-4ef0-bf1e-55b8dba180a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decision: a run whose only unsuccessful jobs never got a runner casts the existing no-label 'cancelled' vote-type (Verified stays 0 after clear-vote; the CANCELLED message and triage comment still post). Precedent: d1d4-8c8b-e2c5-4ac2 (commit b45ce2a490a) made cancelled runs comment-only no-vote outcomes; this reuses that path. ADR 0114 governs adding/promoting required gates and is not engaged: no job enters or leaves the Verified aggregate, and the new snapshot step is continue-on-error input to normalize. Root cause: inside the reusable build-and-test workflow a not-acquired matrix cell does not surface as a 'cancelled' needs result, so FAILURE_OBSERVED=false and the normalize CONCLUSION expression fell through to fail-closed 'failure' (all 4 runs logged CONCLUSION=failure FAILURE_OBSERVED=false -> vote-type=failure). Discriminator (jobs API): runner_id 0, runner_name empty, steps []. Survey of the last 200 Gerrit Verified Gate runs: 19 cancelled jobs matched it, 26 cancelled-after-start jobs all had a runner and 25-29 steps. Auto re-queue rejected: needs actions: write in the job holding the Gerrit vote key. Fail-closed: any other failed/cancelled-with-steps job, FAILURE_OBSERVED=true, or a missing/invalid snapshot keeps Verified -1.","timestamp":1793812279825385001}],"created_at":1793809356101891001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn 2026-11-04 PST, 4 Gerrit Verified Gate runs (41855161578, 41856506741, 41857357120, 41857377497) cast Verified -1 although every job that ran passed. In each run the only unsuccessful job was `build-and-test / pytest (macos-latest, py3.13)`, cancelled with the annotation \"The job was not acquired by Runner of type hosted even after multiple attempts\" plus a macOS arm64 capacity notice. Each change then needed a manual `recheck`. Authors and agents read -1 as a verdict on their change when none exists.\n\n## Root cause (observed)\n- The vote job's normalize step logged `WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION: cancelled` (im-open aggregate), `CONCLUSION: failure`, `FAILURE_OBSERVED: false` -> `vote-type='failure'` in all 4 runs.\n- `FAILURE_OBSERVED` false means no `needs.*.result` was `failure` or `cancelled`, so the `contains(needs.*.result, 'cancelled') && 'cancelled'` branch (`.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`, normalize step `CONCLUSION`) never fired. The reusable `build-and-test` caller result was also not `success`, so the full-route completeness check failed and the expression fell through to its fail-closed `'failure'`.\n- So the no-verdict path added for superseded runs (ticket d1d4-8c8b-e2c5-4ac2, commit b45ce2a490a: \"cancelled -> comment-only no vote\", `scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py` `_VOTE_TYPES[\"cancelled\"]` casts no label) is unreachable when one matrix cell inside a reusable workflow is cancelled.\n- The jobs API distinguishes the cases. Across the 45 cancelled jobs in the last 200 runs, all 19 never-acquired jobs had `runner_id: 0`, `runner_name: \"\"`, `steps: []`; all 26 cancelled-after-start jobs had a runner id and 25-29 steps. No job mixed the two.\n\n## Approach\nFollow the d1d4 precedent: a run whose only unsuccessful jobs were never given a runner carries no test verdict, so it gets the existing `cancelled` vote-type (no label, the existing `CANCELLED: <run url>` message and triage comment; Verified stays 0 after clear-vote). This reuses the existing no-vote path instead of adding a new outcome. Automatic re-queue was not chosen: it needs `actions: write` in a workflow that holds the Gerrit vote key, and d1d4 already fixes the non-verdict semantics.\n\n1. `scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py` (stays one stdlib-only file; `tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port.py::test_entry_point_is_stdlib_only`): add `runner_never_acquired(job)` (conclusion `cancelled`, no steps, no runner id, no runner name) and an optional jobs input read from the file named by `JOBS_FILE`. `normalize()` returns `cancelled` instead of `failure` only when ALL of these hold: conclusion is exactly `failure`, `FAILURE_OBSERVED` is not `true`, the jobs list loads, at least 1 job is a never-acquired cancellation, and every other job except the in-progress vote job (`cast Verified`) concluded `success`, `skipped` or `neutral`. Any missing/unreadable/invalid jobs file, any failed job, or any cancellation with steps or a runner keeps `failure` (fail closed). Existing two-input behaviour is unchanged when `JOBS_FILE` is unset.\n2. `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` vote job: add a `continue-on-error` step before normalize that writes this run's jobs (`gh api --paginate repos/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID/jobs`, already permitted by `actions: read`) to `$RUNNER_TEMP`, and pass that path as `JOBS_FILE` to the normalize step. The script still comes from the trusted default-branch sparse checkout.\n\n## Scope\n- scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py\n- .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml\n- tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_unacquired.py (new)\n- tests/fixtures/ci_jobs/ (new: captured jobs-API payloads)\n- tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py (workflow wiring assertions)\n\n## Testing\nFixtures are captured jobs-API payloads, read-only: run 41855161578 (not-acquired macOS job 126662869315), job 126547335283 from run 41821258615 (cancelled after 29 steps with a runner), and job 126249875159 from run 41731188733 (macOS `failure`, Module-size gate step failed). The mid-test and genuine-failure runs are built by substituting those captured jobs for the macOS job in the 41855161578 job set. Write the tests first and confirm they fail on current main.\n- not-acquired run + `failure` -> `cancelled`\n- mid-test cancellation -> `failure`\n- genuine macOS failure -> `failure`\n- not-acquired plus any other failure -> `failure`; `FAILURE_OBSERVED=true` -> `failure`\n- missing / empty / invalid `JOBS_FILE` -> `failure`; `JOBS_FILE` unset keeps the existing table\n- workflow: the jobs snapshot step precedes normalize, is `continue-on-error`, and normalize receives `JOBS_FILE`\nNo autouse fixtures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A job cancelled because no runner was acquired (no steps executed) does not produce Verified -1 as if tests failed; the chosen behaviour (automatic re-queue of that job, a distinct non-verdict outcome, or another mechanism consistent with ADR 0114 on gating CI) is decided and recorded on this ticket. Checked by the not-acquired fixture test returning `cancelled` and a ticket comment recording the decision and its d1d4 precedent.\n- [ ] A test reproduces the classification from a captured jobs-API payload for a not-acquired cancellation and for a genuine cancellation mid-test, and asserts they are treated differently. Checked by `pytest tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_unacquired.py` passing (and failing on main before the fix).\n- [ ] A genuine macOS test failure still produces Verified -1. Checked by the captured macOS-failure fixture test returning `failure`.\n- [ ] `make lint` (incl. actionlint, zizmor, mechanism and complexity ratchets) and `make typecheck` exit 0, and `pytest tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion.py tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port.py tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` passes.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The fix merges to main through Gerrit at LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; the merged SHA is recorded in a ticket comment. The vote job sparse-checks out these scripts from the default branch, so merging is the deploy.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py","reason":"classify never-acquired-runner cancellations as the no-vote cancelled outcome"},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"snapshot run jobs before normalize and pass JOBS_FILE"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_unacquired.py","reason":"fixture-driven classification tests"},{"path":"tests/fixtures/ci_jobs/","reason":"captured jobs-API payloads"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py","reason":"workflow wiring assertions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py","reason":"find the normalize step by id instead of a fixed index the new snapshot step shifts"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"69021b9d-08e5-4782-ae7f-cd071467185f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"20e1-f766-929b-4951","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Verified -1 when GitHub never assigns the macOS runner","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0c4eba20-5602-475f-a312-feff967d7a19","884ad406-b3d4-4c36-a4c1-e3eeaf418d1f","c13eda7f-fe2e-4d36-8ef1-d53a8e75312d","1a6317c6-84ab-4de1-93ce-33fecd8f2819","69021b9d-08e5-4782-ae7f-cd071467185f","a75094f7-c402-4392-8132-81f00515eabb","8126e3fe-96b8-494c-a404-894a9266cbe5","9ec08129-ccd8-4ef0-bf1e-55b8dba180a7"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793812279825385002,"uuid":"2aa46d93-7cfa-46d1-99f6-44ea86b4eb61"}